#: ../../source/docs/current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling.rst:5
#: 69eacd99331a40afafbd7d1bb0f41283
msgid "Current Limiting and Voltage Scaling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling.rst:7
#: fdd78fe272e54d8ebe6a01743129568b
msgid "Copter includes *current limiting* in order to protect the battery from damage and *voltage scaling* to compensate for the voltage drop as the battery is depleted.  Both of these features require the vehicle to have a :ref:`Power Module or other voltage and current monitor <common-powermodule-landingpage>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling.rst:14
#: 72f0f21afe7346d2b4ea13a46b5a97ef
msgid "Current limiting and voltage scaling were introduced in Copter 3.3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling.rst:18
#: bb904afe8c114f66896a2b52ffc213e7
msgid "Current Limiting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling.rst:20
#: 2d80c4ffe71c4865aac97690e5689ad7
msgid "This protection automatically drops the throttle to as low as 60% of full throttle in order to limit the current requested from the battery. This can be useful to protect the battery from damage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling.rst:24
#: 87518a6dd3aa46dbbde119a2bbbf11a4
msgid "To enable the feature, set the :ref:`MOT_BAT_CURR_MAX<MOT_BAT_CURR_MAX>` parameter to the desired limit in amps (or \"0\" to disable this feature)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling.rst:30
#: 4121724b5ec349649e4655542b630f3c
msgid "If the measured current exceeds this limit the maximum throttle will be reduced to a safe level in 1 to 5 seconds (depending upon how far over the limit it is).  Because the limit can be exceeded for short periods of time, the limit should be set somewhere between the battery's burst limit and its absolute upper limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling.rst:38
#: 0dac346cd00d4d18bf9077af4202c746
msgid "Voltage scaling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling.rst:40
#: 7fcef9a03909450bb08d9fdea2831705
msgid "If enabled, this feature will increase the roll, pitch and yaw control gains to compensate for the voltage drop as a battery is depleted.  This is helpful in that it helps ensure the vehicle's attitude controls do not degrade as the battery weakens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling.rst:45
#: 8ab0c4077d354bffbdf6c745b153a5fb
msgid "To enable set the :ref:`MOT_BAT_VOLT_MAX<MOT_BAT_VOLT_MAX>` to the battery's full charge voltage (i.e. 12.6 for a 3S battery).  Gains will be scaled to attempt to maintain the attitude control response seen at full charge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling.rst:49
#: 2dbf101420cb49ad818eb70e2f7784f2
msgid "Set :ref:`MOT_BAT_VOLT_MIN<MOT_BAT_VOLT_MIN>` to the minimum battery voltage the vehicle would normally experience.  The gains will not be scaled up any more as the voltage falls below this level.  Setting this to the :ref:`battery failsafe voltage <failsafe-battery>` is a good start."
msgstr ""
